WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.922 --> 00:00:10.255
(pop music)

00:00:11.489 --> 00:00:13.960
- So I do work out at mainstream gyms but

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.009
I don't always feel like I fit in.

00:00:16.009 --> 00:00:18.396
- Mainstream gyms are very like machismo

00:00:18.396 --> 00:00:19.380
and aggressive.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.383
- I do go to the gym I

00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:24.007
I have to go into the men's locker room

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:26.695
and you know as somebody that has you know

00:00:26.695 --> 00:00:30.400
a past as a woman going
into an all-male space

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.345
where my you know my body

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:34.567
is very distinctly different

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.558
is terrifying.

00:00:35.558 --> 00:00:38.026
- The gay community puts a lot of pressure

00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:40.208
on men to look a certain way.

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:41.582
And because I don't look that way

00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:44.538
it makes me feel like
something's wrong with my body.

00:00:44.538 --> 00:00:46.359
- This week of working out at a queer gym

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:48.524
is going to be really fun.

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:51.294
(hip hop music)

00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:53.540
- I'm Sam Rypinski and I'm
the founder of Everybody.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.845
- I'm Lake Sharp and I am co-founder.

00:00:55.845 --> 00:00:57.843
- [Sam] Everybody is a radically

00:00:57.843 --> 00:00:59.981
inclusive holistic gym.

00:00:59.981 --> 00:01:02.569
- [Lake] It's a place to build community.

00:01:02.569 --> 00:01:05.858
We welcome you through
our doors as you are.

00:01:05.858 --> 00:01:08.641
You're not required to change anything.

00:01:08.641 --> 00:01:10.595
We welcome your body as it is.

00:01:10.595 --> 00:01:12.528
- Primarily we wanted
to found the gym because

00:01:12.528 --> 00:01:15.651
I wanted a space that I felt
comfortable working out in.

00:01:15.651 --> 00:01:17.796
(hip hop music)

00:01:17.796 --> 00:01:21.103
Hyper body is incredible and is

00:01:21.103 --> 00:01:24.031
exactly what someone from
the future would look like.

00:01:24.031 --> 00:01:25.993
This class does not feel like a

00:01:25.993 --> 00:01:27.759
mainstream gym class

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:29.760
because it takes so

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.239
much from queer culture.

00:01:31.239 --> 00:01:34.264
Bright colors, high energy,

00:01:34.264 --> 00:01:36.958
a slight shamelessness to moving

00:01:36.958 --> 00:01:40.737
that you don't see in mainstream gyms.

00:01:40.737 --> 00:01:42.731
- [Man] I definitely felt like a huge

00:01:42.731 --> 00:01:44.250
sense of belonging.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.031
- [Woman] I did get emotional at one point

00:01:46.031 --> 00:01:47.141
in the class.

00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:49.589
Definitely dancing to Whitney Houston,

00:01:49.589 --> 00:01:51.497
looking around at
everybody and just seeing

00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:52.693
everyone just smile.

00:01:52.693 --> 00:01:54.694
- [Man] I typically
don't like moving my body

00:01:54.694 --> 00:01:55.895
in a sexual manner

00:01:55.895 --> 00:01:58.804
but this class made it okay and I felt

00:01:58.804 --> 00:02:01.653
comfortable to do it and
I felt safe to do it.

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:02.921
(applause)
- [Woman] You guys

00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:04.035
my name is Amelia.

00:02:04.035 --> 00:02:06.500
My preferred gender
pronoun and she/her/hers.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.806
This is Pony Sweat.

00:02:07.806 --> 00:02:10.473
We're gonna move our
bodies for a whole hour.

00:02:10.473 --> 00:02:12.469
- I've always thought I
was a good dancer (laughs)

00:02:12.469 --> 00:02:14.235
until I took Ponies Sweats class.

00:02:14.235 --> 00:02:16.962
There were several times
that I was off beat,

00:02:16.962 --> 00:02:19.796
missing the steps I was
like what is happening here?

00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:21.190
'Cause I can dig it. (laughs)

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.067
- I felt really good when

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.906
she started playing
Robyn's Dancing On My Own.

00:02:26.906 --> 00:02:28.511
- [Man] I'm already not a very good dancer

00:02:28.511 --> 00:02:31.479
so just trying to keep up
I was just like, uhhhhh.

00:02:31.479 --> 00:02:33.266
- Say thank you body.

00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:35.626
(hip hop music)

00:02:35.626 --> 00:02:39.179
Thank you class.
(applause)

00:02:39.179 --> 00:02:41.997
(hip hop music)

00:02:41.997 --> 00:02:43.863
- I thought the class
was a really cool way

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.434
to have a little bit of
a physical interaction

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:50.078
as well as feeling a spiritual
connection to yourself.

00:02:50.078 --> 00:02:51.359
- Today what we're going to do

00:02:51.359 --> 00:02:53.593
is a nice restorative yoga class.

00:02:53.593 --> 00:02:55.744
And we're gonna combine all
the postures with a little

00:02:55.744 --> 00:02:58.884
bit of breath work and mantra.

00:02:58.884 --> 00:03:00.741
- [Woman] The class was super relaxing

00:03:00.741 --> 00:03:03.556
and it felt like a really
good intro into yoga

00:03:03.556 --> 00:03:06.783
in a way of just understanding
and feeling my body more.

00:03:06.783 --> 00:03:09.751
- [ ] Put out a blessing to yourself.

00:03:09.751 --> 00:03:12.051
Send out a prayer to
your friends, your family

00:03:12.051 --> 00:03:14.208
whoever needs your support.

00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:17.461
But again, most of all,
to yourself because

00:03:17.461 --> 00:03:20.302
if you are happy that's
the only way you're

00:03:20.302 --> 00:03:22.144
gonna make other people happy.

00:03:22.144 --> 00:03:24.285
- I knew the classes
were gonna be different.

00:03:24.285 --> 00:03:26.203
I didn't expect them to be so fun.

00:03:26.203 --> 00:03:28.900
- I loved working out at Everybody.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.072
- It was really cool to
just kind of be myself.

00:03:32.072 --> 00:03:35.088
I saw a lot of women
weightlifting which was cool.

00:03:35.088 --> 00:03:36.717
I was like yes, my people.

00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:38.283
- The minute I stepped into Everybody

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:40.551
I saw people who looked like me and I was

00:03:40.551 --> 00:03:41.918
immediately put at ease.

00:03:41.918 --> 00:03:43.954
- Having queer gyms across the country

00:03:43.954 --> 00:03:45.929
would open so many more
people up to fitness

00:03:45.929 --> 00:03:46.762
and that'd be great.

00:03:46.762 --> 00:03:49.222
- If I could send a wish
to myself it would be

00:03:49.222 --> 00:03:53.840
to care for myself and
be patient with my body.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.877
And it's gonna do its own thing.

00:03:55.877 --> 00:03:58.485
I just have to work with it and you know

00:03:58.485 --> 00:04:00.190
love it the way that I can.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.940
(hip hop music)

